  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1136 AM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nThe latest ensemble guidance continue to favor a retrograding high\npressure center going into next week, shifting the main H5 high \nover Texas by Monday, then potentially as far west as New Mexico\nby Wednesday. This will promote a rebound from our slightly \ncooler temperatures over the weekend to more triple digit numbers\nearly to mid next week. Storm chances will also decrease for at\nleast for a day or two as the high moves overhead Monday into \nTuesday, but at least low end chances should return Wednesday into\nlate week as the potential for northwest flow aloft ensues. \n\nWard",
